From 4f5b1dd49c083d35166aa98ddf09edd3274ffb6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:09:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refuse structural reviews before allocating runs
 [daveey]

Unknown-author review admission previously fell through to claimed spawn accounting; ready retries additionally leaked through generic quota preflight. Move typed structural refusal accounting into review-owned preclaim handling, retain bounded visible escalation and home custody, and exempt classified reviews from generic quota resolution. Preserve author history, failure budgets and candidate walls.

Proof: two actual-dispatch unknown-author cases fail before repair (extra run / uncaught refusal); both now pass with no claims, runs or provider launches. Final saved13-file no-retry run:297 passed,2 failed, both new ready-known-author controls whose same-card sdlc-review fixture intentionally suppresses own author evidence. Stop at bounded two iterations; controls retained red for authentic source-linked fixture correction. Full scripts/check --base origin/main passes. No fleet remediation or landing claimed.
